       information. Nowadays, the supply chain of the food system is market-oriented,
       including the whole industrial chain of production, processing, distribution, whole-
                    ：




       sale, retail, consumption and recycling (Amir gharhegozli, 2017). Each link has a
       more or less impact on the eﬃciency of the food system. As the population grows,
       so will the number of people living in cities. Food demand will have to be replen-
                   号




       ished, there will be more orders, food transportation will have to go further, and
       the eﬃciency of the food system will change.
