     • Society and income elasticity
        Income Elasticity refers to the degree of change of demand quantity caused by
        the change of consumer’s income under the condition of constant price and other
        factors. In developed countries, where income increases, demand for expensive
        goods increases rapidly and demand for basic goods such as bread increases only
        marginally. So the income elasticity of demand for these commodities is negative.




