  7    Conclusion
                                          AT
          信




      To sum up, we ﬁrst establish a Basic Food System Model, and then use two superior
  indicators of Equity and Sustainability to optimize the Original Basic Model. Through
  the establishment of index system, the Food System Comprehensive Evaluation Index is
  微

                                    M



  used to measure the stability of food system.
      Greece and Kenya were selected to apply and test the model. Using the collected
                     ：




  data, we ﬁnd that with the Equity and Sustainability, the Score is 0.445 for Greece and
  0.294 for Kenya. Without the Equity and Sustainability, it is 0.423 for Greece and 0.350
  for Kenya. The percentage change is 5.2% and -16.0%, Sensitivity analysis showed that
                    号




  Greece’s Food System was more sensitive to Climate Change, Biodiversity and Gender,
  while Kenya’s Food System was more sensitive to Economic Change.
      When discussing the priority of food system, the indicators in the system are divided
            信




  into two categories: Basic Needs and Higher Pursuit. The Cost-beneﬁt Function is used
  to analyze countries of diﬀerent nature to ﬁnd out the Equilibrium Point. By measuring
      微




  the beneﬁts and cost diﬀerences between developed and developing countries, the impact
  of priority on food systems is discussed. The corresponding parameters of equilibrium
  point of Greece and Kenya are 0.44494 and 0.26847, respectively.
      Improving the scalability of the model by adjusting the framework of the model. For
  the smaller regions, the indicators in the model are reconsidered and weighted, and for
  larger states, the inﬂuence range is limited and the cost is higher due to the diﬃculty of


